            <ArticleTitle>Small bowel involvement documented by capsule endoscopy in Churg-Strauss syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2015.22.41.7810</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Churg-Strauss syndrome is a small and medium vessel vasculitis and is also known as allergic granulomatous angiitis. Gastrointestinal involvement is common in patients with Churg-Strauss syndrome (20-50%). The most common symptoms are abdominal pain, diarrhoea and occasionally gastrointestinal bleeding and perforation. We present a case of Churg-Strauss syndrome with small bowel lesions documented by video capsule endoscopy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
